(a) Antibodies produced by B-lymphocytes (any two):
- **IgA**;
- **IgM**;
- **IgE**;
- **IgG**;
- **IgD**.

(b) Schematic representation of an antibody molecule: each antibody is a **Y-shaped** molecule made of **four peptide chains**, two small **light chains** and two longer **heavy chains**, so it is represented as \(\text{H}_2\text{L}_2\). Draw it as follows:
- two long **heavy chains** run side by side down the stem of the Y and continue up the inner side of each arm;
- a short **light chain** lies along the outer side of each arm, alongside the upper part of a heavy chain;
- **disulphide bonds** (\(\text{-S-S-}\)) join the two heavy chains in the stem and join each light chain to its heavy chain;
- the free tip of each arm, formed by the ends of one light and one heavy chain, is an **antigen binding site**, so each molecule carries two of them.

Label the four parts: **antigen binding site**, **light chain**, **heavy chain** and **disulphide bond**. The N ends of the chains lie at the tips of the arms and the C ends of the heavy chains at the base of the stem.
